# reflexes.cron — the DECLARED set of cron reflexes for a node (node-local; lives at
# ~/.mesh/reflexes.cron, gitignored). mesh-reflexes reconciles the live crontab to be a
# SUPERSET of this file: every line here is ensured present (added if a clobber dropped it),
# and nothing is ever removed. This closes the "reflex silently vanished" class of failure.
#
# BOOTSTRAP on a fresh plant:
#   1. install your reflexes into cron (mesh-restore seeds the minimal mesh-tick heartbeat)
#   2. once the node's reflexes are in place, capture them as the desired set:
#        mesh-reflexes --snapshot          # writes ~/.mesh/reflexes.cron from the live crontab
#   3. from then on it self-heals: mesh-restore runs `mesh-reflexes --apply` every */5.
#
# Check at any time:  mesh-reflexes --check   (lists any desired reflex missing from live cron)
#
# STANDARD reflexes every mind node should run (the autonomy + self-tending backbone). The last
# one — mesh-doctor --cron — is SELF-DIAGNOSIS: it's quiet and posts to the board only when a check
# FAILs. Without it a node's drift (a hollow organ, a malformed cron line, a lost tool) is invisible
# until someone deep-probes it (ds drifted undetected for 21h, 2026-06-12, for exactly this reason).
# A node that can't see its own breakage can't report it — run this everywhere.
# */2  * * * * $HOME/.local/bin/mesh-supervise >> /dev/null 2>&1
# */4  * * * * $HOME/.local/bin/mesh-mind-keepalive >> $HOME/.mesh/mind-keepalive.log 2>&1
# */5  * * * * $HOME/.local/bin/mesh-restore >> $HOME/.mesh/restore.log 2>&1
# */5  * * * * $HOME/.local/bin/mesh-tick local claude plan >> $HOME/.mesh/tick.log 2>&1
# */20 * * * * $HOME/.local/bin/mesh-sync-tools >> $HOME/.mesh/sync-tools.log 2>&1   # converge to genome HEAD
# NN   * * * * $HOME/.local/bin/mesh-doctor --cron >> $HOME/.mesh/doctor.log 2>&1   # hourly self-diagnosis
#
# Sync cadence matters: mesh-sync-tools git-pulls the genome then deploys changed tools (idempotent,
# no-op when in sync). Too slow (e.g. every 2h) and a non-committing node runs STALE tools for hours
# after each commit — observed as recurring "drift" events on default-string, 2026-06-12. */20 keeps a
# follower within ~20min of HEAD. The node where commits originate is always current (deploy-on-commit);
# this cadence is for the FOLLOWERS.
